   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about what you like",
     "texto": [
      "After liker («to like») you use å + infinitive to say what you like doing: Jeg liker å lese («I like to read»). English also uses «to» before the infinitive here, so å works just like English «to».",
      "In Norwegian you can also invite someone with Vil du bli med? («Do you want to come along?»). Bli med is a fixed expression."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
